    "description": "This role involves independently implementing business and technical requirements from Jira tickets to ensure a reliable data foundation for meaningful reports. This includes analyzing data in the data warehouse, creating and optimizing ETL processes, and providing a final reporting table as the basis for visualizations in Power BI or SSRS. The responsibilities also include structured coordination with the frontend team, delivering examples and mockups, and supporting the acceptance process with the requesting party/customer (business department). Main tasks: Ticket management and documentation; Processing Jira tickets (analysis, implementation, documentation); Effort estimation, prioritization, and status maintenance; Documentation in Confluence; Data warehouse analysis and modeling; Analysis of relevant data sources in the data warehouse; Data quality check and mapping of source systems; Definition of data models for reporting; Database development and optimization; Development of SQL queries, views, and stored procedures; Working with Oracle (PL/SQL) and MS SQL Server (T-SQL); Performance optimization; ETL design, implementation, and operation; Conception and implementation of ETL processes; Logging, monitoring, and error handling; Scheduling and performance tuning; Modeling and reporting; Building reporting tables (key figures, metadata, permissions); Working with OLAP structures and SSAS; Ensuring performance, consistency, and traceability; Coordination with frontend development; Collaboration with frontend teams (Power BI / SSRS); Conducting reviews and coordination regarding the data structure; Providing interface descriptions, test data, and validation rules; Review, mockups, and acceptance; Conducting structured reviews for functional validation; Creating sample datasets, SQL examples, and mockups Definition of acceptance criteria including validation rules and performance requirements; support with User Acceptance Testing (UAT); documentation of results and execution of the formal sign-off; quality assurance and support; creation and execution of test cases; conducting peer reviews; monitoring of production processes; support with incident resolution. This role requires close, proactive communication with the requesting party/customer and frontend development, as well as a structured, documented way of working to ensure quality and traceability. The project language is German/English.\n\nSkills: Oracle (PL/SQL), MS SQL Server (T-SQL), SSAS / OLAP, ETL processes, Power BI, SSRS, Jira, Confluence",
